§10.2's range in cell count, against every family the record names

  the tower's own sizes: Λ8 976, Λ9 1,654, Λ10 2,535, Λ11 13,585, Λ12 70,905, Λ13 199,130

  family                                       from        to    ratio   17x?  100x?
  the tower Λ8 to Λ13                           976   199,130    204.0   no    no
  Λ8 to Λ12                                     976    70,905     72.6   no    no
  Λ8 to Λ11                                     976    13,585     13.9   no    no
  Λ8 to Λ10                                     976     2,535      2.6   no    no
  register 1830's six sampled settings          976   234,340    240.1   no    no

  §10.2 prints a 17-fold range; Figure 10.1's caption and the
  appendix row print a 100-fold one, of the same measurement.
  NO family the record names gives either number.

  Register 1830 already recorded why: the base-cap pair population is 475,800,
  no one-parameter cap family from the base sums to the 776,000,000 pairs
  both sentences claim, and the six sampled settings reach 234,340 cells — a 240-fold
  range, not seventeen and not a hundred. The population is not named anywhere.

  So this is not a choice between a right number and a wrong one. Both are unsupported,
  and what the volume owes is the cap family, after which the ratio is arithmetic.

  NOT part of this collision: main L3538's '2.17-fold spread in cell count' is a
  different object — one transition said four ways — and is named here so it is not swept in.
